        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Higgins Creek, Kioloa State Forest, Batemans Bay, Deua National Park, Moruya, Narooma, Congo, New South Wales, Australia\n- Topics: Cortinarius kioloensis type specimen\n\nFacts:\n- The type specimen of Cortinarius kioloensis was collected along Higgins Creek in Kioloa State Forest near Batemans Bay in southern New South Wales on 22 June 1980.\n- Batemans Bay is a town in the South Coast region of New South Wales, Australia.\n- The nearest coastal towns to Deua National Park are Batemans Bay, Moruya, and Narooma.\n- Congo is a village in Eurobodalla Shire on the South Coast of New South Wales.",
